   "meaning": "a statement that is true in every row of its truth table, e.g. A \u2228 \u00acA",
   "ch": 7,
   "short": "Logic",
   "page": 7
  },
  {
   "word": "contradiction",
   "meaning": "a statement that is false in every row of its truth table, e.g. A \u2227 \u00acA",
   "ch": 7,
   "short": "Logic",
   "page": 7
  },
  {
   "word": "implication (if... then)",
   "meaning": "P \u21d2 Q: false only when P is true but Q is false",
   "ch": 7,
   "short": "Logic",
   "page": 8
  },
  {
